# Monorepo environment-variable catalog; all values are intentionally empty.
# Reference only: there is no shared root .env loader or shared environment setup.
# Use each project's .env.example and README; configure only that project's needs.
# Do not copy this union into a child .env: unrelated names can fail validation.
# Remove unused empty entries before loading a child template; empty may override defaults.
# Never commit .env or credentials. Keep existing per-project virtual environments.
# Scope: variables consumed by project source and configurable launchers, including CI.
# Excludes standard OS variables, launcher-local scratch variables and dependency internals.
# CI is process-only: never clear the CI runner's value or add it to project 4's .env.

# Project templates (paths relative to this directory):
# 1-Production-RAG-Pipeline/.env.example
# 2-Structured-Output-Engine/.env.example
# 3-Context-Assembly-Service/.env.example
# 4-LLM-Evaluation-Harness/.env.example
# 5-Semantic-Cache-Layer/.env.example
# 6-Model-Routing-Gateway/.env.example
# 7-Multi-Tenant-LLM-API/.env.example
# 8-Fine-Tuning-Pipeline/.env.example
# 9-Agent-Memory-System/.env.example
# 10-Guardrails-Middleware/.env.example
# 11-Streaming-Response-Infrastructure/.env.example
# 12-Prompt-Versioning-and-AB-System/.env.example
# 13-LLM-Observability-Stack/.env.example
# 14-Tool-Calling-Framework/.env.example
# 15-Self-Correcting-RAG-Agent/.env.example
# 16-Agentic-Document-Extraction/.env.example

